[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11005"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/e1b6599646532be14e417731c4a8b2f7c4dffcc475e2b99cda0279e7dbf08bc6.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-3{x}^{2}+5x$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=1$, shown above." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-3{x}^{2}+5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+5\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{1}+5\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-3(\\frac{1}{3}-0)+5(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-49348"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/bd73ecb5633b2d3e43637ab5be7dacb6cd69d96957fbc199b0d59bbe6dbbcbec.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-1-(1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-54472/selection/db8907708fa965790feda83f90ac435f6577d16ec61ad10c89982cc4e17f2a9a" :answer/id #uuid "a09f0c3b-479f-56be-a220-0c7fc453e356" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=-\\sqrt{3}$, $b=\\sqrt{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54472/selection/c1e60f039fb68e091583c9c1d418216f1f5e92deeed6daca02aa140261567d0a" :answer/id #uuid "23709cc8-86bd-5d54-ad69-e2c7c903069b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=-3$, $b=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54472/selection/08b686ad236b7b360a295e6792554deb7dfe728ae6d07d4a39e703f3169620f5" :answer/id #uuid "d3ef8ea1-c94f-50b7-95ba-dccfb90de2d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=0$, $b=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54472/selection/939afdedfb0df0bde72cef5c5afadf36c0eca0ac3cee50c0e00508e1b2bdc48d" :answer/id #uuid "e32dbc9c-de4e-5a52-a897-a7867eeaa2a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=-1$, $b=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54472/selection/a5271bf30ff4fa1af21dd4b0fd6f8e0c49c5ee134bd34da8a85c32f3945d873b" :answer/id #uuid "c331e181-b4e2-57a3-99f0-ba0dccc61b83" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$a=0$, $b=\\sqrt{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54472/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0510363d-9a97-5539-a060-21b35aa932d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-54472/selection/db8907708fa965790feda83f90ac435f6577d16ec61ad10c89982cc4e17f2a9a" :answer-field/choices ["q-54472/selection/db8907708fa965790feda83f90ac435f6577d16ec61ad10c89982cc4e17f2a9a" "q-54472/selection/c1e60f039fb68e091583c9c1d418216f1f5e92deeed6daca02aa140261567d0a" "q-54472/selection/08b686ad236b7b360a295e6792554deb7dfe728ae6d07d4a39e703f3169620f5" "q-54472/selection/939afdedfb0df0bde72cef5c5afadf36c0eca0ac3cee50c0e00508e1b2bdc48d" "q-54472/selection/a5271bf30ff4fa1af21dd4b0fd6f8e0c49c5ee134bd34da8a85c32f3945d873b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-54472" :question/id #uuid "bca0210a-1680-56db-b343-767175961d1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-54472" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/eb35df379a8d7a20b9003218ee65e1cdcc3849af919805795dab380441d32795.png)\n\nThe area of the shaded region between the curve $y=3-{x}^{2}$ and the $x$-axis is given by the integral expression below. What are the values of $a$ and $b?$\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{a}^{b}(3-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get $a$ and $b$, we need to find the $x$-intercepts of the curve $y=3-{x}^{2}.$ \n\nWe solve the equation for $y=0$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-\\sqrt{3}$ and $b=\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-54472/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-54472"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73329/selection/b8f0e62eab69cdb16a8a3a6ee585ee64ff4e4fceb4750b117ca2bbc5c6e6a4de" :answer/id #uuid "89596ee0-833a-5ab0-9dab-d705437e9a86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi }{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73329/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" :answer/id #uuid "117eeca9-3b82-5db9-98bb-283c60f71050" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73329/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer/id #uuid "b48673d8-0f48-5ae2-9c3c-3de91b9504dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73329/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "514b4be5-6fe3-5aad-8d81-198ee63dcbce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73329/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951" :answer/id #uuid "053e5cc1-0229-5911-98f4-9827337634dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73329/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d0aacdf-3497-57dc-8558-29fd6ca8953b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73329/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" :answer-field/choices ["q-73329/selection/b8f0e62eab69cdb16a8a3a6ee585ee64ff4e4fceb4750b117ca2bbc5c6e6a4de" "q-73329/selection/07a3540ad51bfb53d362c69b0c3835b387a5d7d769d089dc5189f608ec57d640" "q-73329/selection/7b1b8538b264eef6681d0ab5f3b14d51b6cdff67f34fba59d0886ae5c6acf80a" "q-73329/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" "q-73329/selection/986e06f062dcc0ad37fbb185f7e0d56b0fd8e74b571035e7dc0af3d06af89951"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73329" :question/id #uuid "40d8392a-291a-59db-8a83-13f4cd515fda" :question/math-academy-id "q-73329" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/d787ab7b213815ceb2cee11cf3f4a629c0f24b8328b33ae773be1e63f9f9a517.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\frac{2}{1+{x}^{2}}$, the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=1$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{-2}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-2(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73329/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73329"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345320/field-1/1ae3eccf863686446a2a06abd1cf708d9c8fa8120c457b08693fcf7410f01abe" :answer/id #uuid "21b97066-2f2c-5921-8b43-8c652541bd56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345320/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "15d42f86-aed5-5605-85e1-b952c35280a2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-345320/field-1/1ae3eccf863686446a2a06abd1cf708d9c8fa8120c457b08693fcf7410f01abe" :answer-field/choices ["q-345320/field-1/1ae3eccf863686446a2a06abd1cf708d9c8fa8120c457b08693fcf7410f01abe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345320" :question/id #uuid "901a6f11-447b-5c94-9ac6-eec54a15b2b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-345320" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038613/assets/927b979152097aef3939fa78738dbd2deb9d297cadf2d9894c19f31ca76aee1b.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+1$ and the $x$-axis between $x=0$ and $x=\\pi $, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+x){|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\pi )-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+0) \\\\  & =(1+\\pi )-(-1) \\\\  & =\\pi +2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-345320/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345320"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
